{"id": "unknown-2026-11-16-007", "date": "2026-11-16", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 47, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Solar recycling 2.0", "content": "<p>Millions of solar panels will soon reach the end of their useful lives across the globe, not least in the United States where companies are in a race to deploy novel processes to capture and monetize as much material from these modules as they can.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/16/solar-recycling-2-0/\">Solar recycling 2.0</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/16/solar-recycling-2-0/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-16-008", "date": "2026-11-16", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 47, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["installation_demand", "trade_tariff", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.25, "keywords": ["growth", "decline"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Global solar installations face first annual decline in eight years", "content": "<p>China’s shift to market-based tariffs will drive most of this year’s drop in global solar installations, before cheaper batteries help revive growth from 2027, says GlobalData.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/16/global-solar-additions-set-to-fall-for-first-time-since-2018/\">Global solar installations face first annual decline in eight years</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/16/global-solar-additions-set-to-fall-for-first-time-since-2018/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-16-009", "date": "2026-11-16", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 47, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "HoloSolis raises €15 million, welcomes four new shareholders", "content": "<p>The financing will support development of a solar cell and module factory in Hambach, France, with an annual production capacity of 5 GW. The project is expected to create 1,900 jobs, with production scheduled to begin in 2027.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/16/holosolis-raises-e15-million-welcomes-four-new-shareholders/\">HoloSolis raises €15 million, welcomes four new shareholders</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/16/holosolis-raises-e15-million-welcomes-four-new-shareholders/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-16-010", "date": "2026-11-16", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 47, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "AI model detects small fires, smoke in PV plants", "content": "<p>Developed by researchers at China Huaneng Group, the deep-learning framework achieved 87.4% detection accuracy on a PV-specific dataset. It also reduced false alarms caused by sunlight reflections and demonstrated real-time performance on embedded hardware.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/16/ai-model-detects-small-fires-smoke-in-pv-plants/\">AI model detects small fires, smoke in PV plants</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Glob", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/16/ai-model-detects-small-fires-smoke-in-pv-plants/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-16-011", "date": "2026-11-16", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 47, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "PVcase launches early-stage feasibility and design software", "content": "<p>The company’s new PVcase Concept cloud-based software aims to bridge the gap between site selection and detailed engineering by helping developers organize data and get a clear picture of prospective outcomes before making a decision about whether to move ahead with a project.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/16/pvcase-launches-early-stage-feasibility-and-design-software-at-re-2026/\">PVcase launches early-stage feasibility and design software</a> appeared first on ", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/16/pvcase-launches-early-stage-feasibility-and-design-software-at-re-2026/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-16-012", "date": "2026-11-16", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 47, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["strong demand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Octopus Energy launches plug-in solar kit for small businesses", "content": "<p>Octopus Energy has launched plug-in solar kits for small businesses across the UK, following strong demand for its residential offering. The company claims the systems could reduce electricity bills by up to 23%.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/16/octopus-energy-launches-plug-in-solar-kit-for-small-businesses/\">Octopus Energy launches plug-in solar kit for small businesses</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/16/octopus-energy-launches-plug-in-solar-kit-for-small-businesses/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-16-013", "date": "2026-11-16", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 47, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "PV and batteries could help cut global power costs by 40% in 2030s", "content": "<p>A Schneider Electric Research Institute analysis of 40,500 scenarios finds that coordinated investment in distributed solar, battery energy storage and electrified demand could reduce total global electricity system costs by up to 40% in the 2030s, provided technology costs fall as projected. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/16/pv-and-batteries-could-help-cut-global-power-costs-by-40-in-2030s/\">PV and batteries could help cut global power costs by 40% in 2030s</a>", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/16/pv-and-batteries-could-help-cut-global-power-costs-by-40-in-2030s/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-16-014", "date": "2026-11-16", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 47, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Philippines approves solar cell factory from undisclosed investor", "content": "<p>Manila has signed off on a solar cell plant that dwarfs every other project in a state agency’s pipeline this year, as clean energy reshapes the country’s investment flows.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/16/philippines-approves-solar-cell-factory-from-undisclosed-investor/\">Philippines approves solar cell factory from undisclosed investor</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/16/philippines-approves-solar-cell-factory-from-undisclosed-investor/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-16-015", "date": "2026-11-16", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 47, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Solar, wind and batteries can deliver firm power at $0.086/kWh, says Ember", "content": "<p>An analysis by Ember finds that adding wind power to solar PV and battery storage systems reduces the median cost of meeting 90% of electricity demand from $105/MWh to $86/MWh. The cost could fall further to $52/MWh by 2050, based on the regional cost projections used in the model.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/16/solar-wind-and-batteries-can-deliver-firm-power-at-e78-mwh-says-ember/\">Solar, wind and batteries can deliver firm power at $0.086/kWh, says Ember</a>", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/16/solar-wind-and-batteries-can-deliver-firm-power-at-e78-mwh-says-ember/", "type": "rss"}]}
